+# Phase 14.5.51 — Core Operational Localization I
+
+## Objective
+Extend the Phase 14.5.50 localization foundation into the highest-frequency operational workspaces while preserving all existing navigation keys, persisted codes, accounting/inventory behavior and service contracts.
+
+## Localized in this slice
+- Sales main workspace: title, KPIs, credit-policy surface, invoice search/list states, payment/collection presentation and primary actions.
+- Purchases main workspace: title, KPIs, supplier-aging action, invoice search/list states and primary actions.
+- Customer and supplier directories: titles, KPIs, search/empty states, balance/credit summaries and profile-entry actions.
+- Accounting shell: tab labels plus accounting workspace heading.
+- Journal main workspace: KPIs, search, table headings and empty states.
+- Treasury main workspace: KPIs, quick actions, account list states and cash/bank presentation.
+- Inventory main workspace: heading, KPIs, quick actions, section chips, balance filters/search and alert surfaces.
+
+## Resource model
+- English/default strings remain in `values/strings.xml`.
+- Arabic strings remain in `values-ar/strings.xml`.
+- Resource key sets and format placeholders must remain identical.
+- Internal Arabic section/navigation keys that are already behavioral contracts remain unchanged; only their visible labels are localized.
+
+## Safety boundary
+No intended changes to Room entities/schema/migrations, DAO queries, accounting posting/reversal, sales/purchase calculations, inventory quantities/costing, customer/supplier balances, production logic, compensation/commissions, permissions/authentication, backup/restore or other domain/business logic.
+
+## Deferred
+Deep operational dialogs and secondary tabs that still contain direct Kotlin text are intentionally deferred to later localization slices. This phase does not claim 100% whole-app translation.
